  <main id="top">
    <section class="page-hero section-pad"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT SARAH</p><h1>Maps led the way<br />to the <em>ice.</em></h1><p>A geospatial scientist turned glaciologist, Sarah Child studies how glaciers move and change across the polar regions.</p></section>
    <section class="about-detail section-pad"><div class="about-image-wrap"><img src="/sarah-mountain.jpeg" alt="Sarah Child on a mountain overlook in a red jacket" /><span class="image-stamp">A MOUNTAIN MOMENT</span></div><div class="about-detail-copy"><p class="eyebrow">A CAREER IN ICE AND IMAGERY</p><h2>Seeing change<br />across <em>time.</em></h2><p>Sarah Child is a glaciologist and geospatial scientist whose research uses satellite observations, historical imagery, and field measurements to understand glacier dynamics. Her work has focused on multi-decadal change in Antarctica and Greenland, including glacier flow, calving, and grounding-zone behavior.</p><p>She is currently a postdoctoral fellow with the Department of Atmospheric and Environmental Sciences at the University at Albany, SUNY. Previously, she worked with the Cooperative Institute for Research in Environmental Sciences (CIRES) at the University of Colorado Boulder.</p><p>She earned a PhD in Geology from the University of Kansas, an MSc in Geographic Information Science from the University of Edinburgh, and a BS in Geographic Information Systems from SUNY Cortland. Before her research career, she was an All-American field hockey player at Cortland and was inducted into the SUNY Cortland C-Club Hall of Fame in 2022.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.albany.edu/daes/postdoctoral-fellows" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Meet the DAES postdoctoral fellows <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="about-links section-pad"><p class="eyebrow">MORE ABOUT SARAH</p><a href="https://www.albany.edu/daes/postdoctoral-fellows" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">University at Albany profile <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://cires.colorado.edu/people/sarah-child" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Former CIRES profile <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://womeninpolarscience.org/profiles/sarah-child-phd/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Women in Polar Science <span>↗</span></a><a href="https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Sarah-F-Child-2185070386" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ResearchGate publications <span>↗</span></a></section>
